type: software
title: >-
  Emergent quantum mechanics from the TGP substrate: measurement, Born rule,
  superposition, entanglement, spin-statistics, and decoherence from a single
  soliton ODE
abstract: >-
  Preprint and supporting numerical material for the TGP emergent-QM paper,
  companion to the TGP core paper. From the same substrate soliton ODE that
  fixes the TGP core, quantum mechanics is shown to be emergent: the Born rule
  P ~ |psi|^2 from measurement back-reaction asymmetry, superposition as the
  linear limit of the substrate ODE, CHSH = 2*sqrt(2) (Tsirelson) from a
  substrate phasor on pi_3(S^3), spin-1/2 from hedgehog winding B = 1,
  spin-statistics from exchange phase (-1)^B, and decoherence from
  hbar(Phi) damping + non-linear mode mixing + back-reaction.
  Predicted altitude shift Delta-hbar/hbar ~ -3.5e-10 near Earth provides
  a direct atom-interferometry falsification target.
